 Calculation of the sum \[\sum_{i = a, b, c, d, e}\frac{i^4}{\prod_{j\not = i}(i - j)} = \sum_{i = a, b, c, d, e}\frac{i^4}{Q(i)},\] where \[Q(x) = \prod_{j\not = i}(i - j) = (x - b)(x - c)(x - d)(x - e).\] Then the denominator is the same, so we can multiply this out without changing the sum.

Each term in the resulting polynomial will
have a degree less than or equal to 4.
Let'sNow multiply out terms, grouping based on
which of $a, b, c, d,$ or $e$ are included in the denominator. Then we
have
\begin{align*}
&\frac{a^4}{(a - b)(a - c)(a - d)(a - e)} \\
&\quad + \frac{b^4}{(b- a)(b- c)(b - d)(b - e)} 
+ \frac{c^4}{(c- a)(c- b)(c - d)(c - e)} 
+ \frac{d^4}{(d- a)(d- b)(d - c)(d - e)} 
+ \frac{e^4}{(e- a)(e- b)(e - c)(e - d)} \\
&=\frac{(a-b)(a-c)(a-d)(a-e)a^4 + (b-a)(b-c)(b-d)(b-e)b^4}{Q(a)Q(b)} \\
&\quad + \frac{(c-a)(c-b)(c-d)(c-e)c^4 + (d-a)(d-b)(d-c)(d-e)d^4}{Q(c)Q(d)} \\
&\quad + \frac{(e-a)(e-b)(e-c)(e-d)e^4 + (a-b)(a-c)(a-d)(a-e)e^4}{Q(e)Q(a)}. \\
\end{align*}
Each term appears twice each for $x \in \{a, b, c, d,\}$ three times for
$x \in \{b, c, d, e\},$ and four times for $x \in \{c, d, e, a\}.$ By Vieta's
formulas, the evaluation will be
\begin{align*}
&=\frac{4a^5 + b^5 +c^5 + d^5 + e^5}{Q(a)} + \frac{a^5 + 4b^5 + c^5 + d^5}{Q(b)}
+ \frac{a^5 + b^5 + 4c^5 + d^5}{Q(c)}
+ \frac{a^5 + b^5 + c^5 + 4d^5}{Q(d)}
\\
&=\frac{(a^5 + b^5 + c^5 + d^5 + e^5)(a + b + c + d + e)}{Q(a)Q(b)Q(c)Q(d)} \\
&=\frac{(a^5 + b^5 + c^5 + d^5 + e^5)(-7)}{(a - b)(a - c)(a - d)(a - e)} \\
&=\boxed{-7}. \\
\end{align*} </think> -7. </answer>

